they have been providing help to those  in need in our community for 80 years  and counting we're talking about  catholic charities of southern nevada  the sponsors of this segment and joining  us to tell us more about the  organization is senior vp and chief  operating officer steve schmidt hello  steve how are you  good afternoon thank you so much for  having me on it is a pleasure tell us a  little bit about catholic charities what  do you do  well like you said since 1941 as you  mentioned 80 years hard to believe  there's not many things 80 years old in  las vegas but catholic charities of  southern nevada has served those in need  the most vulnerable in the las vegas  valley and through the generosity of our  many foundations grants and many  individual donors our 16 programs and  services have provided support to more  than 4 000 people each and every day i  know that you guys have been doing so  much in the community but you've also  been doing a campus renovation can you  tell me a little bit about that  as you just said we we are undergoing a  major renovation of our eight acre  campus on north las vegas boulevard  where we have been located for over 20  years some people may remember this was  the former vegas village site uh we  recently celebrated the reopening of our  dining hall where we welcome back not  only the nearly 500 guests that we serve  there every day but also volunteers i  know you guys were there on thanksgiving  and christmas to film some of those  events  and now we're currently in the process  of renovating our emergency night  shelter which exists to help 400 adult  homeless men every night of the year and  give them a place to shower and sleep  and we hope to complete this phase in  late spring early summer let's talk a  little bit about that shelter it  how does it help  vulnerable people get back on their feet  our shelter much like the dining hall is  there to serve a fundamental human need  that is food in our and our dining room  and pantry and shelter a place to sleep  but like all our services this isn't a  final destination but a stop along the  way to recovery uh throughout all our  services whether it's our pantry dining  room or shelter we create a safe and  welcoming environment where case  managers who are here at all hours can  get in touch with our clients directly  assess their situation and help them  navigate whatever situation they're in  put them in touch with needed services  mental or behavioral health all with the  goal to get them back on their feet and  become self-sustainable we do that  through all our programs like renewing  hope which helps them with job training  and life skills as well as our housing  navigation center which can help them  get housing or even something as simple  as a bus ticket home that i love that  that it is not a final destination and  you are there just to help them get back  where they need to be now if people want  to help  how do they do that do they where do  they donate  so if your easiest way is to go to our  website we have a number of volunteer  opportunities available including  helping out in our food pantry or  serving our community meal but the most  impactful are monetary donations where  89 cents of every dollar goes directly  to programs and services which helps us  sustain our operations throughout the  year and serve those most in need again  please visit catholiccharities.com to  find out all the ways you can help thank  you for all that you and everyone at  catholic charities for what you do it's  amazing and every donation helps thank  you for your time catholic charities of  southern nevada help them sustain their  operations throughout the year and serve  those in need again for those who can  give at this time please visit  catholiccharities.com or call them at  702-385-2662  kendall
 

